% More decisions of the Medicare Appeals Council, on items of seven modelled
% policies — the transcutaneous electrical joint stimulator (tejsd.le, with
% the TENS supplies of tens.le), negative pressure wound therapy (npwt.le),
% the wearable defibrillator (aeds.le), an ultralightweight manual wheelchair
% (manual_wheelchairs.le), power wheelchairs (pmd.le) — and on two items no
% policy decides: a diabetic alert dog, which the Council found not to be
% durable medical equipment, and a face-down positioning system billed as a
% positioning cushion (E0190), which it found to be (the support surface and
% wheelchair seating policies are included so that the model is seen not to
% decide that code).
%
% One scenario per decision, named after its text file in sources/council/
% ("scenario jdk is, as stated in Council decision jdk:"), written as
% council_pmd.le and council_other.le write theirs: each fact quotes its
% passage ("confer \"...\""), the treating practitioner's findings say
% "according to the treating practitioner", the Council's "according to the
% Council" with the reason it gave. The Council's outcome is NOT a fact: it is
% in the comment above each scenario; the expectation is what the model
% derives, and where it differs the comment says DISAGREES and why — a
% criterion of the LCD the Council applied (the "individual consideration"
% of a lightweight wheelchair under LCD L11465; the Claims Processing
% Manual's two days before discharge) that the current LCD or this model does
% not have, or that the current LCD has and the Council's did not (the
% specialty evaluation and the ATP of an ultralightweight wheelchair); a fact
% the decision does not state (a residence, a weight, the start of the wound
% therapy, a quantity); a code no policy decides (E1399, E0190).
%
% Codes: the decisions cite the codes of their day; where a decision names
% no code the current one is assumed and the comment says so (K0005 for an
% ultralightweight wheelchair, K0823 for a Group 2 standard power wheelchair
% as in council_pmd.le); the NPWT canister codes A6551 and A7000 of 2006 are
% transcribed as the current A7000. Most of these decisions concern many
% beneficiaries named only by number: a scenario transcribes the one or two
% the decision says something about, the others being known only through
% the Council's general holding. Facts the vocabulary cannot express are
% listed in each comment as candidate templates. The fourth query, "dme",
% asks the DME definition of dmepos.le, which two of these decisions turned
% on.

the target language is: prolog.
scenario facts require provenance.

the knowledge base council more includes these resources:
    tejsd,
    tens,
    npwt,
    aeds,
    pmd,
    manual_wheelchairs,
    support_surfaces,
    wheelchair_seating.

the knowledge base council more includes:

